# Research Project — ML for Recurrent Events

**Project:** ML Methods for Recurrent Events with Multiple Types
**Institution:** UNC Chapel Hill | **Branch:** main

## Core Principles

- **Plan first** — enter plan mode before non-trivial tasks; save plans to `quality_reports/plans/`
- **Verify after** — compile/render and confirm output at the end of every task
- **Reproducibility** — `set.seed(YYYYMMDD)`, `here::here()` paths, all results replicable
- **Quality gates** — nothing ships below 80/100
- **[LEARN] tags** — when corrected, save `[LEARN:category] wrong → right` to MEMORY.md

## Folder Structure

```
Research/
├── CLAUDE.MD                    # Project guidance
├── .claude/                     # Rules, skills, agents
├── Bibliography_base.bib       # Centralized bibliography
├── Figures/                     # Shared figures
├── Papers/                      # LaTeX manuscript chapters
├── Preambles/header.tex         # LaTeX headers
├── Quarto/                      # Quarto documents
├── Slides/                      # Presentation slides
├── scripts/R/                   # Shared R helpers, themes, palettes
├── quality_reports/             # Plans, session logs, merge reports
├── explorations/               # Research sandbox (60/100 threshold)
├── comparisons/                 # Sub-project: method comparisons
└── Missing Types/               # Sub-project: missing event types
```

## Commands

```bash
# LaTeX (3-pass XeLaTeX)
cd Papers && TEXINPUTS=../Preambles:$TEXINPUTS xelatex -interaction=nonstopmode file.tex
BIBINPUTS=..:$BIBINPUTS bibtex file
# (repeat xelatex twice more)

# R simulation
Rscript scripts/R/filename.R

# Quality score
python scripts/quality_score.py file
```

## Quality Thresholds

| Score | Gate | Meaning |
|-------|------|---------|
| 80 | Commit | Good enough to save |
| 90 | PR | Ready for deployment |
| 95 | Excellence | Aspirational |

## Sub-Projects

| Sub-Project | Path | Focus |
|-------------|------|-------|
| Comparisons | `comparisons/` | Method comparison simulations |
| Missing Types | `Missing Types/` | Pseudo-observations with missing event types |

**Shared:** `Bibliography_base.bib`, `scripts/R/`, `.claude/rules/`, `Figures/`

**Conventions:** Okabe-Ito palette, `here::here()`, `set.seed(YYYYMMDD)`, figures 300 DPI / white bg

## Workflow Loop

```
Your instruction → [PLAN] if needed → Your approval → [EXECUTE] → [REPORT]
```

**Non-negotiables:** `here::here()` paths, `set.seed(YYYYMMDD)`, Okabe-Ito palette, 300 DPI figures, subject-level bootstrap for recurrent events.
